{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1925","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. We Got Everything Covered!"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given two positive integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to find a string $$$s$$$ such that all possible strings of length $$$n$$$ that can be formed using the first $$$k$$$ lowercase English alphabets occur as a subsequence of $$$s$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple answers, print the one with the smallest length. If there are still multiple answers, you may print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note:"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" A string $$$a$$$ is called a subsequence of another string $$$b$$$ if $$$a$$$ can be obtained by deleting some (possibly zero) characters from $$$b$$$ without changing the order of the remaining characters."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1\\leq t\\leq 676$$$) denoting the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test case consists of a single line of input containing two integers $$$n$$$ ($$$1\\leq n\\leq 26$$$) and $$$k$$$ ($$$1\\leq k\\leq 26$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print a single line containing a single string $$$s$$$ which satisfies the above property. If there are multiple answers, print the one with the smallest length. If there are still multiple answers, you may print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n1 2\n2 1\n2 2\n2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nab\naa\nbaab\nabcbac\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the first test case, there are two strings of length $$$1$$$ which can be formed using the first $$$2$$$ lowercase English alphabets, and they are present in $$$s$$$ as a subsequence as follows: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\texttt{a}: {\\color{red}{\\texttt{a}}}\\texttt{b}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\texttt{b}: \\texttt{a}{\\color{red}{\\texttt{b}}}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the second test case, there is only one string of length $$$2$$$ which can be formed using the first lowercase English alphabet, and it is present in $$$s$$$ as a subsequence as follows: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\texttt{aa}: {\\color{red}{\\texttt{aa}}}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the third test case, there are $$$4$$$ strings of length $$$2$$$ which can be formed using the first $$$2$$$ lowercase English alphabets, and they are present in $$$s$$$ as a subsequence as follows: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\texttt{aa}: \\texttt{b}{\\color{red}{\\texttt{aa}}}\\texttt{b}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\texttt{ab}: \\texttt{ba}{\\color{red}{\\texttt{ab}}}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\texttt{ba}: {\\color{red}{\\texttt{ba}}}\\texttt{ab}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\texttt{bb}: {\\color{red}{\\texttt{b}}}\\texttt{aa}{\\color{red}{\\texttt{b}}}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the fourth test case, there are $$$9$$$ strings of length $$$2$$$ which can be formed using the first $$$3$$$ lowercase English alphabets, and they are present in $$$s$$$ as a subsequence as follows: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\texttt{aa}: {\\color{red}{\\texttt{a}}}\\texttt{bcb}{\\color{red}{\\texttt{a}}}\\texttt{c}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\texttt{ab}: {\\color{red}{\\texttt{ab}}}\\texttt{cbac}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\texttt{ac}: \\texttt{abcb}{\\color{red}{\\texttt{ac}}}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\texttt{ba}: \\texttt{abc}{\\color{red}{\\texttt{ba}}}\\texttt{c}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\texttt{bb}: \\texttt{a}{\\color{red}{\\t